 ## Changelog
+- 2026-10-17 (3): LoD visual fixes after the device screenshots (Pregen works there: compiled and ran). Scratch crate (rustc 1.75, real `lod.rs`): `lod::tests::*` 14 of 14 pass; the full crate still needs a build on the phone / CI. Easiest first.
+    - Snow: from step 2 a snow layer was a full white cube that replaced the cell it lay on (white boxes on crowns and hills at the horizon). Now `fill` drops it at step >= 2 and turns the ground block under it into the snow block (id 80); leaves under it stay green; step 1 is still the 1/8 layer. Test `snow_is_a_thin_layer_near_and_not_a_cube_far` (fails without the change).
+    - Oversized crowns: `pick` kept leaves from ONE child of eight, so every mip level doubled a crown and merged trees into boxes; now two children (logs and solids still 4). `a_mip_rounds_terrain_and_keeps_leaves` changed.
+    - Oversized far terrain: `step_for` 150 / 250 / 400 / 600 (1, 2, 4, 8, 16) -> 150 / 280 / 460 (1, 2, 4, 8): hills beyond 600 blocks were cubes of 16. Cost measured on a generated tile: step 2 = 2.9k quads / 314 KB, step 4 = 0.7k / 72 KB, step 8 = 0.2k / 17 KB; build 3-4 ms each (step 1: 11k quads / 1.2 MB).
+    - Not fixed, UNVERIFIED cause: LoD / real-chunk seam and the hard edge. Checked and ruled out: lighting (flat ground has the same shade and AO 1 in both), the `covered` cut (LoD hides inside the real range minus 3 blocks, so the two overlap). What is left is only the real chunks' corner AO and canopy shade, plants (flowers, tall grass) missing in the LoD, and leaf / grass textures stretched over a whole voxel at step >= 2 (a texel is `step` blocks wide). Needs a screenshot of the exact seam.
 - 2026-10-17 (2): Pregen fixed + faster (screenshot: `Pregen: 0 chunks (tap to stop)` for minutes). Compiled and tested in a Linux scratch crate (rustc 1.75, real `lod.rs` + `world/gen`, stubs for wgpu / atlas / mesh): `lod::tests::*` 12 of 12 pass; the full `mc-rs` crate (wgpu 26) still needs a real build on the phone / CI.
     - Root cause: the single `lod` worker ran `pregen_step` only when its job queue was EMPTY, and `Lod::update` refills `MAX_PENDING` view builds every frame (~510 tiles in view), so the queue was never empty and pre-generation never ran (old code, test `pregen_runs_while_the_view_is_busy`: 0 chunks after 120 s; now 1.3 s).
     - Now: `pregen_threads()` = cores / 2 clamped 1..3 threads `lod-pregen<i>` (Voxy World Gen's `maxActiveTasks`), each with its own generator (made at its first tile). `claim` (`DistanceGraph.findWork`) takes the nearest tile that is neither done nor taken (`Shared::pg`: `done` / `busy`), the thread reads its file or `make_tile`s it with trees and sends `Msg::Made` to the worker, which `accept`s it (real chunks laid over, file written, counted 16 chunks, `made` -> re-mesh). A view build that made the tile first wins. Stops by itself when nothing is left; `Drop for Lod` ends the threads. `Msg::Wake`, `pregen_step` and the `try_recv` branch are gone; `Store::make` is the free `make_tile`.
